course: dictionary
lesson: 16126
title: Whippy: bendy, or soft and fluffy?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word tell you which meaning to use. «The gardener cut a whippy stick from the willow tree.» A stick you can cut from a tree and bend is thin and flexible, so whippy means bending easily and springing back here.
explain: «We bought a cone of Mr Whippy at the seaside.» You eat a cone, and at the seaside it is a treat, so a Mr Whippy must be a soft, creamy ice cream. Here whippy means soft and fluffy, like whipped cream.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. "Bendy and springy" fits «The fishing rod was whippy», but "bendy" does not fit «a cone of Mr bendy». The sentence tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Whippy is an adjective: whippy, whippier, whippiest.
fact: «Whippy» means thin and bending easily, then springing back.
fact: A whippy branch or a whippy fishing rod is flexible, so it bends and springs back.
fact: In the UK, «Mr Whippy» is an informal name for soft-serve ice cream.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, so check the clues in the sentence to find the right one.
exercise: «The willow twigs were whippy, and they sprang back when the wind let go.» What does whippy mean here? | Hard and heavy like a rock | Soft and sweet like cream | *Thin and bending easily, then springing back | Cold and icy
exercise: «We bought a Mr Whippy cone at the seaside.» What kind of thing is a Mr Whippy? | A fishing rod | *A soft, fluffy ice cream | A kind of stone | A tall tree
exercise: Lily says whippy only ever means ice cream. Is she right? | Yes, it only means ice cream | No, it means very cold | Yes, it means a hard, stiff stick | *No, it can also mean bending easily, like a whippy stick
test: «The fishing rod was whippy, so it bent when the fish pulled.» What does whippy mean? | *Flexible, bending and springing back | Very loud | Stiff and unbendable | Sweet and creamy
test: Which sentence uses whippy to mean soft and fluffy? | The branch was whippy in the wind | The stick was whippy and thin | *He ordered a Mr Whippy with a flake | The rod was whippy and bent
exam: What does whippy mean in «The whippy aerial bent over the car roof, then sprang straight again.»? | Hard and fixed in place | Soft and creamy | Cold and wet | *Bending easily, then springing back
